## 38.7 Computed Attributes（Properties）（计算属性 · Properties（property））

### 英文原文

> The example in the prior section simply traces attribute accesses. Usually, though, properties do much more—computing the value of an attribute dynamically when fetched, for instance, as Example 38-2 illustrates.
>
>
> ```python
> Example 38-2.
> ```
>
> prop-computed.py ```python
>
>
> ```python
> class PropSquare:
> def __init__(self, start):
> self.value = start
> def getX(self):
> ```
>
> ``` # On attr fetch ```python return self.value ** 2
>
>
> ```python
> def setX(self, value):
> ```
>
> ``` # On attr assign ```python self.value = value X = property(getX, setX) ``` # No delete or docs ```python P = PropSquare(3) # Two instances of class with property Q = PropSquare(32) ``` # Each has different state information ```python print(P.X) ``` # 3 ** 2 ```python P.X = 4 print(P.X) ``` # 4 ** 2 ```python print(Q.X) ``` # 32 ** 2 (1024) This class defines an attribute X that is accessed as though it were simple data, but really runs code to compute its value when fetched.
>
> The net effect triggers an implicit method call.
>
> When the code is run, the value is stored in the instance as state information, but each time we fetch it via the managed attribute, its value is automatically squared: ```python $ python3 prop-computed.py 9 16 1024 ``` Notice that we’ve made two different instances—because property methods automatically receive a self argument, they have access to the state information stored in instances.
>
> In our case, this means the fetch computes the square of the subject instance’s own data.

### 中文翻译

> The example in the prior section simply traces 属性访问es. 通过示例演示本节机制。 （原文要点：Usually, though, properties do much more—computing the value of an attribute dynamically when fetched, for instance, as Example 38-2 illustrates.）
>
> prop-computed.py ```python
>
> ``` # On attr fetch ```python return self.value ** 2
>
> 讨论 property 如何把属性访问路由到函数。 （原文要点：``` # On attr assign ```python self.value = value X = property(getX, setX) ``` # No delete or docs ```python P = PropSquare(3) # Two instances of class with pr…） The net effect triggers an implicit method call. 讨论 property 如何把属性访问路由到函数。 （原文要点：When the code is run, the value is stored in the instance as state information, but each time we fetch it via the managed attribute, its value is automatically…） In our case, this means the fetch computes the square of the subject 实例’s own data.
>
> （本节另有 3 段代码示例，见英文原文代码块；核心逻辑见「代码分析」。）

### 深度理解

