> 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：``` # On all attribute deletion [del obj.name] In these, self is the subject instance object as usual, name is the string name of the attribute being accessed,…） The two get methods normally return an attribute’s value, and the other two return nothing (None). All can raise exceptions to signal prohibited access.
>
> 通过示例演示本节机制。 （原文要点：For example, to catch every attribute fetch, we can use either of the first two previous methods, and to catch every attribute assignment we can use the third.） The following uses __getattr__ ```python for fetches:
>
> 说明 `__getattribute__` 拦截所有读取及递归风险。 （原文要点：``` X.job # Prints "Get: job"X.pay # Prints "Get: pay"```python X.pay = 'bread'``` # Prints "Set: pay bread"Using __getattribute__ works exactly the same in th…）
>
> ``` # On all 属性读取 ```python
>
> 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：``` # Works same as getattr here ```python print('Get:', name) ``` # But prone to loops in general ```python … ``` rest unchanged ```python … ``` Such a coding…） 用校验案例对比不同属性管理技术。 （原文要点：Because all attributes are routed to interception methods generically, we can validate and pass them along to embedded, managed objects.） 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：As a refresher, the following class, borrowed from Chapter 31, traces every attribute fetch made to another object passed to the wrapper (proxy) class: ```pyth…）
>
> ``` # Save object ```python
>
> 讨论描述符协议及其与 property/slots 的关系。 （原文要点：``` # Trace fetch ```python return getattr(self.wrapped, attrname) ``` # Delegate fetch ```python X = Wrapper([1, 2, 3]) ``` X.append(4) # Prints "Trace: appen…） 通过示例演示本节机制。 （原文要点：On the other hand, when such generality is not required, generic accessor methods may incur additional calls for assignments in some contexts—a trade-off descr…）
>
> Avoiding loops in 属性拦截 methods These methods are generally straightforward to use.
>
> Their most complex aspect is the potential for looping (a.k.a. recursing). 说明 `__getattr__` 仅在查找失败后触发。 （原文要点：Because __getattr__ is called for undefined attributes only, it can freely fetch other attributes within its own code.） 说明 `__getattribute__` 拦截所有读取及递归风险。 （原文要点：However, because __getattribute__ and __setattr__ are run for all attributes, their code must be careful when accessing other attributes to avoid calling thems…）
>
> 说明 `__getattribute__` 拦截所有读取及递归风险。 （原文要点：For example, another attribute fetch run inside a __getattribute__ method’s code like the following will trigger __getattribute__ again—and the code will usual…）
>
> ``` x = self.other # LOOPS! 说明 `__getattribute__` 拦截所有读取及递归风险。 （原文要点：Technically, this method is even more loop-prone than this may imply—a self attribute reference run anywhere in a class that defines this method will trigger _…）
>
> 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：This is normally desired behavior—intercepting every attribute fetch is this method’s purpose, after all—but you should be aware that this method catches all a…） When coded within __getattribute__ itself, this almost always causes a loop.
>
> 解释设计动机与适用场景。 （原文要点：To avoid this loop, route the fetch through a higher superclass instead to skip this level’s version—because the object class is always a superclass to every c…）
>
> 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：``` # Force higher to avoid me For __setattr__, the situation is similar, as summarized in Chapter 30 — assigning any attribute inside this method triggers __s…）
>
> 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：``` # Recurs (and might LOOP!) Here too, self attribute assignments anywhere in a class defining this method trigger __setattr__ as well, though the potential …） 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：To work around this problem, you can assign the attribute as a key in the instance’s __dict__ namespace dictionary instead.） This avoids direct 属性赋值: ```python
>
> 说明 `__getattribute__` 拦截所有读取及递归风险。 （原文要点：``` # Use attr dict to avoid me Alternatively, __setattr__ can also pass its own attribute assignments to a higher superclass to avoid looping, just like __get…） 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：In fact, this scheme is sometimes preferred when wrapped classes use slots, properties, or other “virtual” attributes that live on classes instead of instances…）
>
> 通过示例演示本节机制。 （原文要点：``` object.__setattr__(self, 'other', value) # Force higher to avoid me This book’s __setattr__ examples often use __dict__ for smaller demos anyhow, just beca…） By contrast, though, we cannot use the __dict__ trick to avoid loops in __getattribute__: ```python
>
> ``` # Loops! 说明 `__getattribute__` 拦截所有读取及递归风险。 （原文要点：If this is coded, fetching the __dict__ attribute itself triggers __getattribute__ again—causing a recursive loop and an immediate fail.） Strange but true! 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：The __delattr__ method is less commonly used in practice, but when it is, it is called for every attribute deletion, just as __setattr__ is called for every at…） 展开本节技术细节。 （原文要点：When using this method, you must avoid loops when deleting attributes by the same techniques: namespace dictionaries operations or superclass method calls.）
